   \]
   where \( p \) represents all possible values of \( X \), and \( P(X = p) \) is the probability of \( X \) taking the value \( p \).  

2. **Given \( \mathbb{E}(X^2) = 0 \)**:  
   \[
   \sum_{p} p^2 \cdot P(X = p) = 0
   \]

3. **Non-Negativity of \( p^2 \)**:  
   \[
   p^2 \geq 0 \quad \text{for all } p \in \mathbb{R}
   \]

4. **Non-Negativity of \( P(X = p) \)**:  
   \[
   P(X = p) \geq 0 \quad \text{for all } p \in \mathbb{R}

\]

5. **Combining the above**:  
