Relative speed = 45 km/hr - 9 km/hr = 36 km/hr

Now, we need to convert this relative speed to meters per second (m/s). To convert kilometers to meters, we multiply by 1000, and to convert hours to seconds, we divide by 3600.

Relative speed in m/s = 36 km/hr * (1000 meters / 1000 kilometers) * (1 hour / 3600 seconds)
Relative speed in m/s = 36 * (1000 / 3600) m/s
Relative speed in m/s = 36 * (5 / 18) m/s
Relative speed in m/s = 10 m/s

Now, we know that the train takes 25 seconds to pass the jogger. This means that the train covers the distance it have the jogger before the train reaches the jogger and the distance it has the jogger before the train reaches the gate.

