\[
\text{Reaction Time} = \text{Flow Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Velocity}}
\]

1. **Calculate the Flow Velocity**:
   - The volume flow rate is given as 10 cm³/m/L.
   - The radius of the tunnel is \( r = 0.1 \, \text{m} / 2 = 0.05 \, \text{m} \).
   - The area of the tunnel is \( A = \pi r^2 = \pi (0.0005 \, \text{m})^2 \approx 0.787 \, \text{m}^2 \).
   - The velocity is \( v = \frac{\text{Volume Flow Rate}}{\text{Area}} = \frac{10 \, \text{cm}^3 / \text{m}}{ 0.787 \, \text{m}^2} = \frac{10 \, \text{cm}^3 / \text{min}}{ 0.787 \, \text{m}^2} \approx 12.7 \, \text{km/s} \).

2. **Calculate Reaction Times for Different Distances**:
   - For \( d = 1 \, \text{cm} \):
     \[
     \text{Reaction Time} = \frac{1 \, \text{cm}}{12.7 \, \text{km/s}} = \frac{0.001 \, \text{m}}{12700 \, \text{m/s}} \approx 0.78 \text{ seconds}
     \]
   - For \( d = 10 \, \text{cm} \):
     \[
     \text{Response Time} = \frac{10 \, \text{cm}}{12.7 \, \text{km/s}} = \frac{0.01 \, \text{m}}{12700 \, \text{m/s}} \approx 0.78 \text{seconds}
     \]

**Final Answer**:
