","To compute the natural frequencies and mode states for the binary-layer double-layer double-layer-free-free-type system, we can use the matrix equation:

\[
\left( \begin{bmatrix} \left( \frac{m_t}{m_t} + \frac{k_t}{m_t} \right) & \frac{k_c}{m_t} \\ \frac{k_c}{m_t} & \left( \frac{m_t}{m_t} + \frac{k_t}{m_t} \right) \end{array} \right) \left( \begin{bmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \end{{bmatrix} \right) = \frac{m_t}{m_t} \left( \begin{bmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \end{bmatrix} \right)
\]

For \( N = 3 \) blocks, the matrix equation becomes:

\[
\left( \begin{bmatrix} \left( 1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t} \right) & \frac{K_c}{m_t} & \frac{K_c}{m_t} \\ \frac{K_c}{m_t} & \left( 1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t} \right} & \frac{K_c}{m_t} \\ \frac{K_c}{m_t} & \frac{K_c}{m_t} & \left( 1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t} \right) \end{pmatrix} \right) \left( \begin{bmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \\ x_3 \end{bmatrix} \right) = \frac{m_t}{m_t} \left( \begin{bmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \\ x_3 \end{bmatrix} \right)
\]

This can be rewritten as:

\[
\left( \left(1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t}\right)I + \frac{K_c}{m_t}I \right)x = \frac{m_t}{m_t} x
\]

where \( I \) is the identity matrix.

**Step 1: Compute the Eigen Eigenvalue Equation**

The equation simplifies to:

\[
\left( \left(1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t}\right)I + \frac{K_c}{m_t}I \right)x = \frac{m_t}{m_t} x \implies \left( \left(1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t}\right)I + \frac{K_c}{m_t}I \right)x = 1 x
\]

This can be rewritten as:

\[
\left( \left(1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t}\right)I + \frac{K_c}{m_t}I \right)x = \frac{1}{m_t} x
\]

This is a homogeneous equation with eigenvalues \( \lambda \) and eigenvectors \( x \):

\[
\left( \left(1 + \frac{k_t}{m_t}\right)E + \frac{K_c}{m_t}E - \frac{1}{m_t}E \right)x = 0
\]

