1. **Identify the triangle:** We have an isosceles triangle with base 20 units and two equal sides of 13 units.
2. **Identify the height:** The height of the triangle is the perpendicular line from the vertex opposite the base to the base. This height bisects the base of the isosceles triangle into two equal parts.
3. **Identify the right triangle:** The height creates two right triangles within the isosceles triangle. Each right triangle has a hypotenuse of 15 units (one of the equal sides of the isosceles triangle) and one leg of half the base, which is half of 20 units, which is 10 units.
